    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a calculated offensive approach, headlined by **Junior Caminero** (66.09) and **Christian Yelich** (64.16), who grade out as our most efficient starts. **Junior Caminero** benefits from a favorable matchup against Soriano, J, enjoying a solid base projection that is bolstered by a productive spot in the four-hole. Meanwhile, **Christian Yelich** earns his elite status by leveraging a massive 13% boost from his dynamic platoon advantage against the right-handed Nola, A. With the Zebras prioritizing stolen base potential, **Christian Yelich** remains a focal point of our strategy; while he faces an elite hold pitcher, the projected run production from his leadoff position is too significant to ignore in our quest for 5x5 category dominance.\n\nThe toughest decision on today\u2019s card involved **Carson Benge** (52.34), who nearly cracked the lineup but ultimately fell just short of the efficiency thresholds maintained by the likes of **Nelson Velazquez** (52.51) and **Luke Raley** (53.21). While **Carson Benge** offers upside against P\u00e9rez, M, the optimizer favored the platoon advantages of our current outfield mix. We are exercising caution with **Caleb Durbin** (44.04), whose score is suppressed by a high-risk matchup against deGrom; despite his high speed profile, the lack of SP-specific efficiency limits his role today. We continue to monitor the status of **Colt Keith**, who remains sidelined, and have successfully stashed **Hyeseong Kim** in the minors to maintain roster flexibility. Management will be watching the weather closely, as several of our starters are facing high-strikeout threats; ensure **Dillon Dingler** and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** remain prepared for the specific defensive tendencies of the opposing catchers, as those marginal gains are critical in tight roto races.",
